WEBVTT

01:36.820 --> 01:39.360
Hello, my beloved glasses wearers!

01:39.520 --> 01:40.560
Feeling good?

01:40.780 --> 01:42.580
My name is Soma Akira,

01:42.580 --> 01:44.790
second year at Himaraya
3rd Technical High School

01:44.790 --> 01:46.380
and president of the Glasses Club.

01:46.380 --> 01:49.650
Our Glasses Club is hard at work
on our dream glasses,

01:49.650 --> 01:54.010
X-Ray Glasses that let their wearer
see through anything.

01:54.450 --> 01:58.550
We've hit walls, we've suffered,
we've shed tears...

01:58.550 --> 02:04.010
But we have many allies, and
teachers who watch out for us.

02:04.010 --> 02:07.730
That's right! Our classmates,
the school, the people of the city,

02:07.730 --> 02:10.680
they all support and encourage us!

02:11.230 --> 02:14.410
And now we know for sure.

02:14.410 --> 02:18.880
That now, it is our Glasses Club
that makes the world go 'round!

02:19.380 --> 02:21.710
And on the day when the
hearts of the Glasses Club

02:21.710 --> 02:23.750
were about to become one
with those of all mankind,

02:23.750 --> 02:25.720
they came forward.

02:25.720 --> 02:28.770
The Himaraya 3rd Technical
High School Student Council...

02:28.770 --> 02:30.470
Hima Council, for short.

02:30.960 --> 02:35.640
The Hima Council has taken numerous
cowardly measures to try to eliminate us.

02:35.640 --> 02:38.630
I admit that at times,
our glasses clouded over,

02:38.630 --> 02:41.080
and our love for glasses faded.

02:41.080 --> 02:44.640
But it was a mistake to feel that way!

02:45.020 --> 02:48.980
Our love for glasses will not
yield to the Hima Council!

02:48.980 --> 02:49.980
That's right!

02:49.980 --> 02:56.820
The world's glasses will send a rainbow
of hope and courage to our hearts!

02:56.820 --> 02:59.720
Now, observe closely.

02:59.720 --> 03:03.660
Starting now, the Glasses
Club gets serious!

03:08.720 --> 03:11.330
Getting hungry just before you fall asleep.

03:11.940 --> 03:13.660
It happens, doesn't it?

03:14.200 --> 03:18.010
You wonder if you should prepare that
instant ramen you happen to have,

03:14.860 --> 03:15.650
Instant Ramen

03:15.770 --> 03:16.650
Boil

03:18.010 --> 03:21.200
or endure the hunger and go to sleep.

03:18.400 --> 03:20.820
Hunger

03:20.820 --> 03:21.570
Sleep

03:21.200 --> 03:23.190
It's a truly difficult decision.

03:21.570 --> 03:23.190
Difficult

03:24.420 --> 03:29.000
If you choose to eat the ramen,
take great care.

03:29.000 --> 03:31.560
Your glasses may fog over,
making it difficult to see.

03:31.560 --> 03:35.490
But if you take off your glasses,
it's even harder to see.

03:37.560 --> 03:42.560
As Long as My Glasses Sparkle,
You Won't Get Away with It!

03:42.560 --> 03:45.590
Lunch Break

03:49.100 --> 03:51.740
Ta-da! Special Glasses Bento!

03:51.740 --> 03:54.170
Time to ea—

03:57.730 --> 04:00.260
It's so realistic, I can't eat it!

04:00.650 --> 04:02.100
Kugishima Sachie's "The Healthy Boy's Lunch"
Special Edition: Glasses Bento

04:02.280 --> 04:05.810
But it really does look like him.

04:06.290 --> 04:09.980
Okay! Maybe I'll hit the
cafeteria for a change!

04:09.980 --> 04:12.540
School Store

04:12.850 --> 04:13.760
Student       Student       Student

04:13.760 --> 04:14.710
Hayato

04:15.080 --> 04:19.220
Oh, please! To the great Hayato-sama,
this isn't just a piece of cake,

04:19.220 --> 04:21.510
it's a piece of cake with ice cream on top!

04:21.930 --> 04:22.870
Tsk.

04:28.960 --> 04:30.730
Takuma-senpai!

04:34.010 --> 04:35.940
Cafeteria

04:38.500 --> 04:40.880
I wonder if they have
anything with avocado...

04:38.500 --> 04:41.880
Tickets

04:43.840 --> 04:46.970
Soma-senpai, can I eat with you?

04:48.490 --> 04:49.380
Huh?

04:51.130 --> 04:54.120
Soma-senpai, aren't you going to eat?

04:52.450 --> 04:52.930
Eat

04:54.120 --> 04:56.440
It'll go to waste. Eat it.

04:56.440 --> 04:57.530
But...

04:57.680 --> 04:59.100
I'm leaving it up to you.

05:00.030 --> 05:03.530
<i>Is this... Soma-senpai's leftovers?</i>

05:03.920 --> 05:05.910
Soma-senpai's leftovers

05:04.140 --> 05:05.900
Down the hatch!

05:05.910 --> 05:09.900
Soma-senpai

05:12.070 --> 05:14.130
So good!

05:14.130 --> 05:14.910
Huh?

05:16.040 --> 05:18.720
Yukiya-senpai! There's an open seat here.

05:20.330 --> 05:22.220
No, thank you.

05:22.660 --> 05:24.520
Oh, okay...

05:34.160 --> 05:35.520
Glasses?

05:35.520 --> 05:38.260
Glasses Club Room

05:36.850 --> 05:38.270
Good work toda—

05:38.270 --> 05:39.440
Huh?!

05:39.440 --> 05:42.490
X-Ray-Ray! X-Ray-Ray!

05:46.610 --> 05:48.620
Zzz...

05:48.210 --> 05:52.370
E-Everyone's swapped personalities!

05:53.370 --> 05:54.060
And so...

05:54.770 --> 05:56.920
What exactly happened?

05:55.390 --> 05:56.580
What

05:58.020 --> 06:02.130
New at Store

05:58.020 --> 06:02.130
Cream Puffs

05:58.020 --> 06:02.130
New Type

05:58.240 --> 06:02.130
I went to buy some cream puffs
and they had a new type out.

06:02.130 --> 06:05.120
New Type
Russian Cream Puff

06:02.390 --> 06:05.140
I'll have this one, this one, and that one!

06:06.630 --> 06:10.010
It's a new type! Russian cream puffs!

06:10.210 --> 06:13.640
Will it taste like strawberry?
Or like chocolate?

06:19.450 --> 06:23.440
What

06:19.830 --> 06:23.440
What is this? Leaves? Soy sauce?

06:23.610 --> 06:25.000
Leaves

06:23.610 --> 06:25.000
Soy sauce

06:23.730 --> 06:26.900
Spinach boiled in soy. Very austere.

06:27.360 --> 06:29.650
That's the "bad draw," right?

06:30.080 --> 06:33.120
The other two were spinach, too.

06:33.630 --> 06:37.110
All three were?
Those are some amazing odds.

06:37.110 --> 06:39.920
And that's why you were
working on the X-Ray Glasses?

06:41.070 --> 06:43.840
I'm after the strawberry flavor!

06:44.360 --> 06:46.960
What happened to you, Yukiya-senpai?

06:47.570 --> 06:52.770
Me? I was spending lunch
time as I usually do.

06:53.570 --> 06:55.930
I ordered omelet rice as usual.

06:56.280 --> 06:58.400
I headed for my usual seat.

07:00.660 --> 07:03.180
<i>Why is there a bust here?</i>

07:04.150 --> 07:08.070
<i>Was it left there by accident?
Is someone saving the seat?</i>

07:08.070 --> 07:09.650
I was naïve.

07:10.220 --> 07:12.920
Since I sit in the same place every day,

07:12.920 --> 07:16.990
I fell under the delusion
that it was "my place."

07:15.640 --> 07:16.990
Delusion

07:17.190 --> 07:19.040
Why were you doing leg lifts?

07:19.040 --> 07:21.360
If I could get to the cafeteria
faster than anyone,

07:21.360 --> 07:23.840
then no one could take my seat.

07:24.090 --> 07:26.330
I could secure "my place" for myself.

07:26.540 --> 07:27.810
I see.

07:27.810 --> 07:30.110
I guess my turn is next.

07:28.590 --> 07:29.990
Next

07:30.990 --> 07:35.350
Kimata Hayato faces the
greatest trial of his life!

07:35.630 --> 07:36.940
Don't push me!

07:36.940 --> 07:38.610
It's coming! They only make one every day!

07:38.610 --> 07:40.110
The extra-large daifuku anpan!

07:40.110 --> 07:41.360
Extra Large Daifuku Anpan

07:41.440 --> 07:44.850
Oh, please! To the great Hayato-sama,
this isn't just a piece of cake,

07:44.850 --> 07:46.610
it's a piece of cake with ice cream on top!

07:53.000 --> 07:55.300
And if I get it again tomorrow,

07:55.300 --> 07:58.990
I'll set a new extra-large daifuku
anpan consecutive grab record!

07:59.420 --> 08:01.750
Only one <i>and</i> number one!

08:05.960 --> 08:07.910
But I still won't lose!

08:08.480 --> 08:10.070
As a Glasses Club representative,

08:10.070 --> 08:13.560
I <i>must</i> heal up and take
the record tomorrow!

08:13.560 --> 08:16.420
And once I do, I'll become
an official club mem—

08:16.920 --> 08:18.930
Nobody's listening!

08:19.360 --> 08:23.240
Soma-senpai, what were you
looking up on the yPad?

08:23.480 --> 08:28.820
Why did only I get a small
portion of curry rice?

08:24.570 --> 08:28.820
I wanted to find out why I was the only one
who got a small portion of curry rice.

08:28.980 --> 08:31.380
Oh, no!

08:30.320 --> 08:37.330
Empty

08:31.380 --> 08:34.020
I planned to eat just a little bit
when I got hungry early,

08:34.020 --> 08:37.320
but I ended up eating it all before lunch!

08:39.210 --> 08:41.680
Nothing wrong with eating in
the cafeteria now and then.

08:39.210 --> 08:45.000
Tickets

08:41.680 --> 08:44.520
The lack of omelet katsu-rice
is lamentable, but...

08:45.000 --> 08:47.500
Ramen would cloud up my glasses.

08:45.000 --> 08:47.500
Ramen

08:47.500 --> 08:50.560
Curry udon has the danger of
splattering broth on my glasses.

08:47.500 --> 08:50.560
Curry Udon

08:50.820 --> 08:53.280
I settled on simple curry rice.

08:52.550 --> 08:53.920
Curry Rice

08:54.340 --> 08:57.300
When it comes to school lunch,
volume is more important than taste.

08:57.300 --> 08:59.980
To provide significant
volume for the price

08:59.980 --> 09:02.310
and satisfy the needs of growing boys...

09:02.310 --> 09:06.250
A mountain of curry rice,
piled high...

09:02.310 --> 09:06.250
A sea of curry roux about to
overflow from the plate

09:02.310 --> 09:06.330
One could say that is the mission
bestowed upon the school cafeteria!

09:08.210 --> 09:09.820
S-So small!

09:11.730 --> 09:14.020
Where is my mountain
of rice piled to the sky?

09:14.020 --> 09:17.650
Where is my sea of curry roux
about to overflow from the plate?

09:20.500 --> 09:21.580
Why?

09:21.580 --> 09:24.870
Why am I the only one with
a small portion of curry rice?!

09:26.330 --> 09:28.380
So it wasn't leftovers after all?

09:28.680 --> 09:30.960
So, did you find your answer?

09:31.420 --> 09:32.130
No.

09:32.140 --> 09:34.890
Why did only I get a small portion of curry rice?

09:32.140 --> 09:34.890
Search Results: 0

09:32.560 --> 09:34.880
Even the yPad threw in the towel.

09:34.880 --> 09:37.860
There are things even the
yPad doesn't know.

09:37.860 --> 09:39.950
The Earth is truly vast.

09:39.950 --> 09:43.280
It sounds like everyone was
unlucky at lunch today.

09:44.560 --> 09:46.820
At times like these, we need
the ultrasonic cleaner!

09:46.820 --> 09:50.400
Unclouded lenses will drive away the
evil spirits and call in good fortune!

09:50.400 --> 09:53.160
That's our Soma-senpai! Let's go do it!

09:53.160 --> 09:55.610
But Mitsuki, nothing bad happened to y—

09:55.880 --> 09:58.870
Hayato, you're not resting at all, are you?

09:59.660 --> 10:00.660
Okay.

10:01.540 --> 10:04.170
Let's ultrasonic even harder than usual!

10:04.170 --> 10:06.130
Let's add a bit of hot water.

10:06.130 --> 10:09.460
Lukewarm water cleans
lenses easier than cold.

10:09.460 --> 10:12.770
I pray that I'll get strawberry
flavor tomorrow!

10:17.720 --> 10:19.450
Eggplants? Why?

10:20.360 --> 10:22.010
And four of them?

10:22.550 --> 10:25.520
Four eggplants. Four "nasu."

10:26.090 --> 10:27.450
"Shi" nasu.

10:28.270 --> 10:29.570
Shinasu?!

10:28.660 --> 10:29.560
Shinasu = I'll kill you

10:29.570 --> 10:31.060
Th-This means...

10:31.700 --> 10:34.560
What happened to the Glasses Club
wasn't just simple bad luck.

10:34.560 --> 10:37.680
It was someone's clever set-up!

10:37.680 --> 10:40.120
These eggplants are their
declaration of responsibility.

10:40.670 --> 10:43.410
Culprit

10:41.010 --> 10:43.410
I will find the culprit!

10:43.880 --> 10:45.940
I swear it on the name of the Glasses Club!

11:00.090 --> 11:03.180
This is who I represent.

11:03.640 --> 11:04.890
Might I have

11:05.060 --> 11:06.620
a moment of your time?

11:05.060 --> 11:07.520
Great Detective Mitsuki

11:08.380 --> 11:10.370
A suspicious character?

11:11.190 --> 11:12.780
There was no one like that here.

11:12.780 --> 11:15.060
Please, try to remember!

11:16.170 --> 11:17.800
I'm telling you, there was no one like that.

11:17.800 --> 11:19.610
This is a cafeteria, you know.

11:18.300 --> 11:19.610
Cafeteria

11:20.160 --> 11:22.820
If anyone suspicious came here,
I would run them out.

11:22.820 --> 11:25.280
Th-That is true!

11:22.890 --> 11:23.680
Scary

11:25.780 --> 11:28.590
Thank you for your cooperation!

11:28.970 --> 11:30.490
Wait a minute.

11:29.060 --> 11:29.730
Wait

11:30.490 --> 11:32.300
Take this with you.

11:32.300 --> 11:34.840
Th-Thank you...

11:32.730 --> 11:34.840
What?

11:38.760 --> 11:42.020
One's favorite food is an
important source of energy.

11:44.350 --> 11:45.810
Proper Enunciation

11:44.350 --> 11:45.810
Ah

11:45.810 --> 11:49.180
Crime Scene Investigator Mitsuki

11:46.840 --> 11:48.890
This should reveal any fingerprints.

11:51.580 --> 11:59.910
powder    powder    powder    powder

11:59.910 --> 12:00.700
Forensic Analyst Mitsuki

12:01.740 --> 12:05.840
No eyewitness testimony. No fingerprints.

12:05.840 --> 12:08.580
Traditional Vegetable
Yoshikawa Eggplants

12:06.530 --> 12:08.280
Our only clue is eggplants.

12:09.360 --> 12:10.660
At times like these...

12:12.430 --> 12:14.300
I'm counting on you, Norio-san!

12:21.400 --> 12:22.380
Time passes...

12:22.380 --> 12:23.820
Open

12:26.170 --> 12:28.140
The culprit is here?

12:29.820 --> 12:31.560
Yes? Come in.

12:32.330 --> 12:33.490
Excuse me.

12:33.600 --> 12:35.740
Oh, Kamatani-san.

12:35.740 --> 12:37.940
It's unusual to see you here.

12:38.900 --> 12:46.650
Criminal Investigator Mitsuki

12:38.920 --> 12:41.020
Where were you today at lunchtime?

12:41.540 --> 12:43.600
Where did this come from?

12:43.600 --> 12:46.050
Is there something you
don't want to tell me?

12:46.050 --> 12:49.440
O-Of course not.

12:49.440 --> 12:51.660
At lunchtime, I was...

12:51.660 --> 12:52.680
Well...

12:52.680 --> 12:54.380
<i>Look at him squirm!</i>

12:54.890 --> 12:56.280
<i>There's no question!</i>

13:05.680 --> 13:09.190
confess   confess   confess

13:05.970 --> 13:08.900
Confess to everything and
we'll go easy on you.

13:09.180 --> 13:10.690
I can't tell him.

13:09.660 --> 13:10.690
I can't tell him.

13:11.380 --> 13:13.530
We held a club budget
meeting at lunchtime,

13:13.530 --> 13:16.380
and resolved to give the Glasses Club
by far the lowest budget of them all.

13:16.380 --> 13:19.310
They're stuck with 500 yen again.

13:19.970 --> 13:22.470
How am I supposed to
reveal that heartless truth

13:22.470 --> 13:24.700
to a Glasses Club member?!

13:25.030 --> 13:27.260
You revealed it just now.

13:27.260 --> 13:29.200
Just thinking about it gives me...

13:29.200 --> 13:30.530
stomach pain...

13:29.330 --> 13:30.780
Stomach Pain

13:31.330 --> 13:33.400
Your lies won't save you!

13:33.400 --> 13:36.330
Everyone knows the student
council had a motive!

13:36.330 --> 13:40.620
You played this cowardly trick in order to
break the spirits of the Glasses Club!

13:41.140 --> 13:45.140
But as long as Kamatani Mitsuki's glasses
sparkle, you won't get away with it!

13:47.560 --> 13:49.020
It's not a lie.

13:50.750 --> 13:55.220
The Glasses Club advisor was
present at the meeting. Ask him.

13:56.610 --> 14:00.110
The budget meeting this
afternoon? I was there.

14:00.600 --> 14:03.630
The student council members
were all in attendance.

14:03.630 --> 14:04.610
Murmur...

14:04.610 --> 14:06.190
Objection! If I may!

14:06.200 --> 14:13.920
Attorney Mitsuki

14:06.570 --> 14:08.740
There must be time unaccounted for!

14:08.740 --> 14:12.840
Was there any member who
left the room for lunch?

14:13.240 --> 14:17.640
No, they had bread and rice
balls and stuff brought in,

14:13.920 --> 14:19.950
Alibi

14:17.640 --> 14:19.970
and they all ate in the
student council room.

14:19.970 --> 14:21.520
Time Unaccounted For

14:19.970 --> 14:24.340
And... you're positive they were
the real student council members?

14:24.340 --> 14:27.680
All their moles in the right places,
and all using the correct dominant hands?

14:28.010 --> 14:30.420
Of course. What are you talking about?

14:30.550 --> 14:32.220
Um... um...

14:30.570 --> 14:31.010
Hidden Room Trick

14:30.820 --> 14:31.570
Eggplant

14:31.030 --> 14:31.820
Art

14:32.010 --> 14:32.970
Avocado

14:32.470 --> 14:33.220
Banana

14:32.510 --> 14:34.680
There's got to be some trick to it!

14:32.970 --> 14:33.680
40s Era Sailor Suit

14:33.470 --> 14:34.220
Time Displacement Trick

14:33.850 --> 14:34.430
Double Roles

14:34.310 --> 14:34.680
Red Shoes

14:34.520 --> 14:34.680
Performance Fee

14:35.850 --> 14:38.230
Oh! I know! The student council members...

14:38.230 --> 14:40.270
...all have identical twins!

14:42.150 --> 14:43.980
That would never happen.

14:49.660 --> 14:52.950
They have the motive,
but their alibi is rock-solid.

14:53.700 --> 14:56.950
Which means the culprit must not
be from the student council.

14:57.250 --> 14:59.370
The investigation's back to square one.

15:00.120 --> 15:02.880
What are you doing, Norio-san?

15:04.170 --> 15:05.340
That's...

15:06.840 --> 15:09.760
<i>One's favorite food is an
important source of energy.</i>

15:12.430 --> 15:14.010
How did she...

15:14.890 --> 15:17.730
<i>Why did she say that to me, back then?</i>

15:16.520 --> 15:18.140
Small Portion Curry

15:17.270 --> 15:18.270
Statue

15:18.310 --> 15:19.480
Cream puffs

15:19.160 --> 15:19.600
Mystery

15:20.230 --> 15:23.230
Truth

15:21.270 --> 15:23.230
Of course! So that's it!

15:23.860 --> 15:27.990
Mystery                                                         Small Portion
Curry

15:23.860 --> 15:27.990
Statue                                                                     Cream
Puffs

15:24.440 --> 15:26.360
This mystery is solved!

15:30.990 --> 15:33.660
You're saying all our
bad luck at lunchtime...

15:33.660 --> 15:36.450
...was someone's clever set-up?

15:36.450 --> 15:38.750
Could someone really arrange all of that?

15:38.870 --> 15:43.880
Yes. Someone who knows all the favorite
foods and habits of the Glasses Club

15:40.910 --> 15:41.420
Favorite Foods

15:41.750 --> 15:42.250
Habits

15:43.880 --> 15:44.880
Crime

15:43.880 --> 15:45.880
could have committed the crime.

15:46.050 --> 15:48.670
Someone who knows us... like Shirogane?

15:49.210 --> 15:52.010
The Hima Council seems to have
done a lot of digging on us, too.

15:52.010 --> 15:54.390
And there's all the members
of the Glasses Club.

15:55.180 --> 15:56.510
There is

15:56.510 --> 15:57.930
one other!

16:00.770 --> 16:03.190
What are you talking about now?

16:03.190 --> 16:05.190
It's no use playing innocent.

16:05.190 --> 16:06.690
You told me,

16:06.690 --> 16:09.780
"One's favorite food is an
important source of energy."

16:11.070 --> 16:12.700
Right?

16:13.160 --> 16:16.910
And then, just as you said,
inside that bag was...

16:17.160 --> 16:20.910
Avocado Sandwich         Avocado Sandwich

16:17.300 --> 16:20.920
My favorite food, avocado sandwiches!

16:21.250 --> 16:23.370
If you know the favorite food
of someone like me,

16:23.370 --> 16:25.290
who only rarely visits the cafeteria,

16:25.290 --> 16:28.670
you would naturally know the favorite
foods of all the Glasses Club members.

16:28.840 --> 16:33.180
In addition, a lunch lady like you
would be able to commit the crime

16:33.180 --> 16:34.840
without a lot of searching around.

16:34.840 --> 16:35.640
In other words...

16:35.890 --> 16:38.720
Culprit

16:36.180 --> 16:38.890
The one who gave a small portion
of curry to Soma-senpai,

16:39.770 --> 16:42.020
Culprit

16:39.890 --> 16:42.180
stole Yukiya-senpai's seat,

16:43.270 --> 16:46.610
Culprit

16:43.690 --> 16:46.560
and swapped out Takuma-senpai's cream puffs

16:48.190 --> 16:49.400
was you!

16:53.650 --> 16:56.530
Yes. I did all that.

16:57.490 --> 16:58.990
I-Impossible!

16:58.990 --> 17:02.290
But why? Why would you do that?

17:02.290 --> 17:06.170
I was only doing what a lunch lady should.

17:09.920 --> 17:13.510
It looks like you haven't eaten
your avocado sandwiches yet.

17:13.510 --> 17:15.430
You must be starving.

17:15.760 --> 17:17.890
Y-You're...

17:18.930 --> 17:20.140
Kugishima Sachie's "The Healthy Boy's Lunch"
Special Edition: Glasses Bento

17:20.720 --> 17:21.970
Kugishima Sachie.

17:22.600 --> 17:26.060
She's spent 40 consecutive years as
a lunch lady at a boys' high school.

17:26.060 --> 17:28.980
She has satisfied the appetites
of over 10,000 students,

17:28.980 --> 17:31.780
and has, through bespectacled eyes,

17:31.780 --> 17:35.650
observed the "favorite foods,"
"necessary energy,"

17:35.650 --> 17:38.910
and "stomach conditions" of her students,

17:38.910 --> 17:41.410
earning her a reputation as
a legendary lunch lady.

17:41.410 --> 17:43.870
To ensure student health and happiness,

17:43.870 --> 17:46.120
she is finally publishing the top secret recipes

17:46.120 --> 17:48.170
she has been honing for over forty years.

17:48.500 --> 17:50.500
Can it really be you?

17:51.130 --> 17:53.920
I never knew you were
working at our school!

17:54.300 --> 17:57.380
Incidentally, for the Glasses
Bento character model,

17:56.970 --> 18:01.890
Glasses Bento

17:57.380 --> 18:01.890
I used you, the boy who
never shuts up about glasses.

18:02.470 --> 18:04.640
But why did you do all this?

18:06.690 --> 18:08.020
Listen.

18:08.310 --> 18:11.270
It's important to maintain
a good balance in your diet.

18:11.730 --> 18:16.150
You can't just eat sweets all the time.
You must consider proper nutrition.

18:16.490 --> 18:18.860
You won't grow up to be
a fine man if you don't.

18:20.120 --> 18:22.120
You shouldn't always eat in
the shadow of a pillar.

18:22.120 --> 18:24.910
Eat in a place that gets
some sun now and then.

18:24.910 --> 18:27.960
It will even change the taste
of your omelet rice.

18:29.750 --> 18:31.090
If you eat during class,

18:31.090 --> 18:34.170
then eat a large portion of
curry rice on top of that,

18:34.170 --> 18:35.960
it's too many calories,
even for a growing boy.

18:35.960 --> 18:38.720
Curry has far more calories
than you'd think, after all.

18:41.140 --> 18:44.520
So you did all of that for us?

18:44.520 --> 18:48.230
I never considered the beneficial
properties of sunlight.

18:48.230 --> 18:49.560
Now that you mention it,

18:49.560 --> 18:52.820
my brothers are always telling me
that I should eat more vegetables.

18:55.150 --> 18:57.950
Glasses!

19:01.200 --> 19:04.160
You look like you haven't had lunch yet.

19:13.460 --> 19:15.090
There's an open seat here.

19:27.890 --> 19:31.650
Huh? I feel like we're forgetting something.

19:29.140 --> 19:32.400
What?

19:32.650 --> 19:36.530
Must rest, must rest, must rest...

19:36.730 --> 19:39.030
Must rest, must rest, must rest...

19:37.480 --> 19:39.030
Just your imagination.

19:39.190 --> 19:41.610
I see. Just my imagination.

19:41.610 --> 19:43.450
Okay, let's go!

19:43.450 --> 19:45.030
Let's eat!

19:49.250 --> 19:52.330
Food is a thing of limitless depth.

19:52.330 --> 19:55.590
What matters isn't just what you eat,

19:53.290 --> 19:54.790
What

19:55.590 --> 19:59.050
but where you eat it,
and who you eat it with.

19:55.840 --> 19:57.590
Location

19:57.590 --> 19:59.050
Location                                                          Company

19:59.170 --> 20:03.260
But it's easy for people to
make mistakes at times.

20:03.260 --> 20:04.800
That's why, sometimes,

20:04.800 --> 20:10.930
it might be best to have someone like
that lunch lady around to meddle.

20:11.480 --> 20:13.690
Kamatani Mitsuki, signing off.

20:18.190 --> 20:22.200
By the way, what was up
with those eggplants?

20:23.450 --> 20:24.660
Oh, well!

20:26.950 --> 20:28.580
One more truth!

20:32.580 --> 20:35.790
Why does a second year like me
have to buy all this stuff?

20:39.920 --> 20:41.260
Extra Large Daifuku Anpan

20:42.680 --> 20:45.010
Extra large daifuku anpan, eh?

20:45.010 --> 20:49.390
Despite being a second year,
I've yet to have a chance to eat one.

20:49.560 --> 20:53.730
That first year from the Glasses Club
appears to be getting close to the record.

20:57.900 --> 21:01.820
I hope he slips on the
banana peel and falls!

21:02.570 --> 21:03.650
Just kidding.

21:03.650 --> 21:06.280
Only one <i>and</i> number one!

21:10.120 --> 21:13.000
Scream

21:14.870 --> 21:17.330
I didn't go out and buy them
especially for this.

21:17.330 --> 21:19.420
I just happened to have
eggplants on hand.

21:19.420 --> 21:21.420
And I happened to remember my grandpa

21:21.420 --> 21:27.930
saying that putting eggplant slices
on a sprain could help to heal it.

21:27.930 --> 21:31.310
And I just happened to be passing
in front of the Glasses Club room.

21:32.430 --> 21:33.890
Just happened to...

21:38.480 --> 21:39.610
Huh?

23:10.910 --> 23:23.210
Glasses Monument

23:12.120 --> 23:12.950
Have you heard, Mitsuki?

23:12.950 --> 23:13.490
Have you heard, Mitsuki?                                Station

23:12.950 --> 23:14.790
If you put your glasses
on the Glasses Monument

23:13.490 --> 23:17.430
Station

23:14.790 --> 23:16.450
near the station,
your wish will be granted!

23:15.450 --> 23:20.080
Your wish will be granted.

23:16.450 --> 23:17.450
Really?

23:17.450 --> 23:18.460
It's a true special request!

23:17.660 --> 23:19.040
Special request.

23:18.460 --> 23:19.940
That's "special" with the
"spec" from "spectacles."

23:19.040 --> 23:21.500
(Spec)ial request!!

23:19.940 --> 23:20.930
Let's go right away!

23:20.870 --> 23:22.330
Let's go right away!
Let's go right now!

23:20.920 --> 23:21.790
Let's go right now!

23:21.790 --> 23:23.210
Let's go, you and me!

23:23.210 --> 23:25.920
No Glasses, No Life

23:31.010 --> 23:34.140
Wellington. Tomorrow's horoscope:

23:34.140 --> 23:37.020
If you put cream puffs in your
pocket and bump into them,

23:37.020 --> 23:39.450
they'll get crushed, so be careful.
